    passageEn: 'Every drop of water on our globe participates in an endless closed loop known as the hydrologic water cycle. Solar radiation warms vast tropical seas, transforming liquid water into invisible floating vapor during evaporation. As humid air ascends into cooler atmospheric altitudes, water vapor condenses around dust particles to form billowy clouds. When condensing droplets become too dense to remain suspended, gravity releases them as precipitation: rain, sleet, hail, or snow. Runoff streams eventually return toward oceans, perpetuating the planet\'s life-giving circulation.',
